{"base_rate":0.3136482939632546,"brier":0.15056902887139106,"bss":0.30056718801251237,"bss_hi":0.39088114870128393,"bss_lo":0.19597337329030673,"country":"FR","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.11165354330708663,"ess":461.2913556370604,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Montpellier</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Montpellier rain forecast is moderately skilful, though 5 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (100%), believe about\n<b>89%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>8%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 762 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nMONTPELLIER-AEROPORT, 8.0 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.30, ranked 59 of\n109 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(38&ndash;90) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>8%</b></td><td class='num'>373</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>8%</td><td class='num'><b>19%</b></td><td class='num'>73</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>26%</td><td class='num'><b>44%</b></td><td class='num'>87</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>61%</td><td class='num'><b>53%</b></td><td class='num'>73</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>88%</td><td class='num'><b>59%</b></td><td class='num'>66</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>100%</td><td class='num'><b>89%</b></td><td class='num'>90</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">5 of 6 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Montpellier</b> <span class=\"muted\">FR</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag ok\">Moderately skilful</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">5 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.30</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>38&ndash;90\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 109</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>762 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Montpellier &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Montpellier\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"59.13887399463807,378.0965147453083 86.90191780821918,327.1506849315069 149.7958620689655,256.48275862068965 272.77616438356165,122.71232876712332 368.3936363636364,34.545454545454504 410.584,18.0 410.584,26.088888888888903 368.3936363636364,89.69696969696969 272.77616438356165,202.49315068493152 149.7958620689655,319.2413793103448 86.90191780821918,372.027397260274 59.13887399463807,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"267.8320209973753\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"267.8320209973753\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"59.13887399463807,353.69973190348526 86.90191780821918,312.1917808219178 149.7958620689655,223.01149425287355 272.77616438356165,187.53424657534245 368.3936363636364,166.9090909090909 410.584,58.44444444444446\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 8% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 373 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"59.13887399463807\" cy=\"353.69973190348526\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 8%&amp;#10;It rained 19% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 73 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"86.90191780821918\" cy=\"312.1917808219178\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 26%&amp;#10;It rained 44% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 87 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"149.7958620689655\" cy=\"223.01149425287355\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 61%&amp;#10;It rained 53% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 73 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"272.77616438356165\" cy=\"187.53424657534245\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 88%&amp;#10;It rained 59% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 66 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"368.3936363636364\" cy=\"166.9090909090909\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 100%&amp;#10;It rained 89% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 90 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"410.584\" cy=\"58.44444444444446\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(31%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Montpellier the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>spring</b> (0.34) and least in\n<b>autumn</b> (0.17).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>30%</td><td class='num'>0.169</td><td class='num'>11.2%</td></tr><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>184</td><td class='num'>21%</td><td class='num'>0.295</td><td class='num'>6.1%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>39%</td><td class='num'>0.325</td><td class='num'>11.1%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>218</td><td class='num'>34%</td><td class='num'>0.337</td><td class='num'>10.7%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":43.61093,"lon":3.87635,"n":762,"n_cities":109,"name":"Montpellier","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.05,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.0032171581769436996,"n":373,"obs":0.0777479892761394,"sig":true},{"hi":0.15,"lo":0.05,"mean":0.08164383561643836,"n":73,"obs":0.1917808219178082,"sig":true},{"hi":0.4440000000000009,"lo":0.15,"mean":0.25931034482758614,"n":87,"obs":0.4367816091954023,"sig":true},{"hi":0.8,"lo":0.4440000000000009,"mean":0.6067123287671232,"n":73,"obs":0.5342465753424658,"sig":false},{"hi":0.98,"lo":0.8,"mean":0.8768181818181819,"n":66,"obs":0.5909090909090909,"sig":true},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.98,"mean":0.996